@startuml
title Authentication — as-built: Firebase client + backend verify + JIT provisioning

actor User as U
participant "auth screens\n(login/signup/reset)" as Screen
participant "AuthProvider\n(FirebaseAuth SDK)" as FB
participant "Dio _AuthInterceptor\n(api_client.dart)" as Dio
participant "AuthMiddleware\n(auth.go)" as MW
participant "FirebaseAuthService\n(Admin SDK)" as Admin
database "users" as DB

== Client auth (email/password) ==
U -> Screen : sign up / log in / reset
Screen -> FB : createUser / signIn / sendPasswordResetEmail
FB --> Screen : Firebase user (session persisted by SDK)\nno email-verification gate (D2)

== Every API request ==
Screen -> Dio : call API
Dio -> FB : getIdToken() (SDK silently refreshes ~1h token)
Dio -> MW : Authorization: Bearer <token>
MW -> MW : extract Bearer (401 if missing/malformed)
MW -> Admin : VerifyIDToken(token)
note right of Admin : uses VerifyIDToken, NOT ...AndCheckRevoked\n-> revoked/signed-out token valid until expiry ~1h (D1)
Admin --> MW : {UID, email} (401 on failure)
MW -> DB : FindByFirebaseUID(uid)
alt new user (JIT)
  MW -> DB : NewUser(uid, email) Role=OWNER PlanTier=FREE
  MW -> MW : provision personal org (non-blocking, #14)
else DB error (non-notfound)
  MW --> Dio : 503 (logged only, D3)
end
MW -> MW : put *User in context
MW --> Screen : handler runs ; GET /api/v1/me returns current user
Dio -> Dio : on 401 -> FirebaseAuth.signOut()

note over MW
  Route protection is FAIL-CLOSED (verified): every route group guarded by
  `&& cfg.AuthMW != nil` with registration INSIDE -> if Firebase unconfigured,
  routes are NOT registered (404), never open. (positive finding)
end note
@enduml
